![Occupancy, admission rate and abandonment vs demand](figures/occupancy_vs_demand.png)

Full per-point tables (mean ± 95% CI over 5 seeds) are in §10.1. Every run satisfies
Little's law: time-averaged occupancy / (admission rate · E) lies between
{{sim.little_min|f:3}} and {{sim.little_max|f:3}}.

**Two regimes.**

* *Demand-limited:* every attempt is eventually admitted, and occupancy equals
  λ_fresh · E. At C = 5000 this holds up to 1 fresh attempt/s:
  {{demand.C5000-fresh1.time_avg_occupancy|ci:0}} ads, admission fraction
  {{demand.C5000-fresh1.admit_fraction|f:3}}, no abandonment.
* *Waiting-time-limited:* above that, occupancy saturates and extra demand is turned
  away. At C = 1000 this regime already holds at 0.5 attempts/s:

| fresh attempts/s | occupancy / C | admissions/s | abandoned / fresh | `REGTOPIC` per admission |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| {{demand.C1000-fresh0.5.fresh_attempt_rps|f:2}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh0.5.utilisation|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh0.5.admission_rps|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh0.5.abandon_fraction|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh0.5.requests_per_admission|f:1}} |
| {{demand.C1000-fresh5.fresh_attempt_rps|f:0}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh5.utilisation|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh5.admission_rps|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh5.abandon_fraction|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh5.requests_per_admission|f:1}} |
| {{demand.C1000-fresh100.fresh_attempt_rps|f:0}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh100.utilisation|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh100.admission_rps|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh100.abandon_fraction|ci:3}} | {{demand.C1000-fresh100.requests_per_admission|f:1}} |

**Why the cache saturates near a quarter of C.** The production client gives up once
its quoted waits exceed 1.5·E. Admission therefore stops growing at the occupancy u
where a typical first quote reaches 1.5·E. Ignoring lower bounds and the 1 s floor, the
implemented wait is 0.1·E·(x + s)/(1 − u)^10, with topic share x = T/(N+1) and IP score
s. This gives

    u* = 1 − ((x + s) / 15)^(1/10)

which is {{model.ustar.0.25|pct:1}}, {{model.ustar.0.5|pct:1}}, {{model.ustar.1.0|pct:1}} and
{{model.ustar.2.0|pct:1}} for x + s = 0.25, 0.5, 1 and 2. The measured equilibria of
{{demand.C1000-fresh2.utilisation|pct:1}}–{{demand.C1000-fresh100.utilisation|pct:1}} (C = 1000) and
{{demand.C5000-fresh2.utilisation|pct:1}}–{{demand.C5000-fresh100.utilisation|pct:1}} (C = 5000) fall in this
range. Because of the 10th root, the equilibrium hardly depends on demand, on C, or on
the workload (§6.5).

**Waiting.**

* Admitted advertisers waited a median of {{demand.C1000-fresh5.cumwait_waited_median_s|f:0}} s
  (p95 {{demand.C1000-fresh5.cumwait_waited_p95_s|f:0}} s) at the baseline. Most
  admissions happen shortly before the 1350 s attempt timeout.
* At the baseline, {{demand.C1000-fresh5.single_quote_share|pct:0}} of abandonments come
  from a single quote above 1.5·E; the rest from the sum of quotes.
* The p95 quoted wait is {{demand.C1000-fresh5.quoted_wait_p95_s|f:0}} s. Quotes above E
  are common because the registrar does not cap them (D5).
* No wrapped waits occurred. No retry missed its ticket window; in simulated mode this
  holds by construction.

**Topic diversity.** The service term flattens the topic distribution. At the
baseline, the most popular topic holds {{demand.C1000-fresh5.top_topic_population_share|pct:1}}
of the advertisers but only {{demand.C1000-fresh5.top_topic_cache_share|ci:3}} of the
cache. The largest topic list seen during measurement has
{{demand.C1000-fresh5.max_topic_ads|f:0}} ads at the C = 1000 baseline and
{{demand.C5000-fresh100.max_topic_ads|f:0}} at C = 5000 with 100 fresh attempts/s
(mean over seeds). These T values are what the
per-operation costs of §6.1 should be read at.

![Occupancy vs capacity](figures/occupancy_vs_capacity.png)

**Capacity.** Over C = 500 … 10,000 (§10.1, `capacity`) the occupancy fraction stays
between {{capacity.C10000-fresh5.utilisation|pct:1}} and {{capacity.C500-fresh20.utilisation|pct:1}}. The
admission rate scales with C:
* {{capacity.C500-fresh20.admission_rps|f:2}}/s at C = 500;
* {{capacity.C10000-fresh20.admission_rps|f:2}}/s at C = 10,000.
